Gentlemen,
Find attached my synthesis of our discussion from the most recent faculty
meeting. Let me know what you think.

What we provisionally agreed to:
1. The Capstone course, especially for EC/CC, MBAP, one year, undergrad
business.
2. Continuing to flesh out the poster session idea.
a. Poster sessions will be on social science research day (SSRD),
conditional on university acceptance.
b. Poster sessions may include outside community members as a networking
event.
c. The quantitative rubric will be something like three elements;
presentation/communication (broken into constituent elements such as
presentation/poster quality, etc.), specific disciplines with identified
topics/ideas, and logical consistency/integration.
d. There may be a written submission evaluated as well; this was raised but
I forgot to highlight it in the provisional vote.
e. By construction, we will NOT be able to focus exclusively on our own
areas during evaluation; I stated that we would be able to focus this way
and it was pointed out that this is unlikely to be true.
3. Tim is empowered, with support from an as yet unnamed faculty member, to
take ownership of inviting outside evaluators. The objective function here
is still underspecified; we may want former students, current employers,
etc.

If you gentlemen agree with this synthesis, please just let me know. I
think that the next step, if we agree, is to distribute a version of this
to Romana and then the faculty for clarity. Then, if there are no strong
complaints, we move on to build a prototype (likely with Jim) of the
project, presentation and evaluation, including rubrics.

Please let me know your thoughts. Because he volunteered for this task,
I've included Tim on this email to make sure he's not being referenced
without his knowledge.

Best,
-Jon C Thompson

